  "summary": "This paper conducts an empirical partial-identification study on operational weather ensemble forecasts (ECMWF IFS and AIFS-ENS, 50 perturbed members, 28 matched initialization dates in June–September 2026). For 12-site spatial portfolios, it uses linear programming (Hailperin atom bounds over the 4,096 states in {0,1}^12) to compute sharp lower and upper bounds on the tail probability q_k = P(S >= k) that at least k locations exceed a fixed dry-bulb temperature threshold under three nested information releases: (1) individual site exceedance probabilities, (2) individual probabilities plus the aggregate second binomial moment E[S(S-1)/2], and (3) individual probabilities plus all 66 pairwise co-exceedance probabilities. Across 2,871 non-trivial ('informative') queries, mean compatible probability interval widths are 0.5139 (marginals), 0.3146 (marginals + aggregate second moment, capturing 43.4% of the marginal-to-pair narrowing from a single scalar), and 0.0547 (marginals + pairs). Crucially, through systematic sensitivity analyses, the paper demonstrates that the apparent near-identification by pairwise moments (and exact identification in 37.2% of informative queries) is largely an artifact of exact zero pair counts in a finite 50-member ensemble pruning the surviving binary support: pair bounds widen substantially as ensemble size increases from 10 to 25 to 50 members (from 0.0023 to 0.0219 to 0.0547) or when moments are perturbed by 0.005 under continuous weights (widening from 0.0514 to 0.1858), whereas enforcing the 1/50 integer-weight lattice makes a 0.005 tolerance exact-count equivalent. The paper also compares release-only cost–loss action certification, point reconstructions (independence, historical forecast-rank copula, and interval midpoints), subset queries, and bit-level payload sizes against exact task-specific summaries (the 144-bit portfolio count distribution and 600-bit coherent binary mask). Overall, while the geographical scope and 2^n LP scaling are limited to stylized 12-site portfolios and the prose is heavily burdened by defensive audit-log caveats and exploratory add-ons, the mathematical execution, self-skeptical diagnostics, and reproducibility are exemplary.",
